# QA automation hard bans

Applies to **Cursor Automation webhooks**, **לימוד גוקו**, and any **qa-teach-plan-implement** run.

## Before any code edit

1. Read `.cursor/rules/conversation-fix-playbook.mdc` and `.cursor/rules/structured-vs-llm-routing.mdc`.
2. Name the fix layer (prompt → hints → tool guard → pending pre-turn → runtime).
3. If ambiguous Hebrew policy or fix necessity → **AskQuestion** / `ask_operator` verdict — do not guess.
4. **Implement only when required** — skip nice-to-haves, style tweaks, and speculative hardening.

## Allowed first (preferred)

| Layer | Files |
|-------|-------|
| LLM teaching | `lib/hom-agent/prompts/hom-bot.md` |
| Turn hints | `lib/hom-agent/conversation-hints.ts` |
| Tool / thread guards | `lib/hom-agent/tools/*.ts`, `lib/agents/order-lookup.ts`, `lib/agents/service-intake.ts` |
| Pending bind only | `lib/hom-agent/pre-turn.ts` — **existing** helpers only |
| Lock behavior | `lib/hom-agent/__tests__/`, `lib/agents/__tests__/` |

## Hard bans (guard + playbook)

- **No reply sanitizers** — no new/edited `sanitize*`, no stripping in `validate-reply.ts`.
- **No new Hebrew intent regex on customer text** — no `/קבלה/`, `/כן.*תודה/` arms in `off-topic.ts`, `digital-document-flow.ts`, `order-lookup.ts`, etc.
- **No new structured pre-turn arms** — no `runStructured*PreTurn` that re-decides intent from customer wording.
- **No hijacking flows** — thread-state guards only, not keyword-on-latest-line routing.
- **No docs the operator did not ask for** (except `BRIEF.md` / `commit-log.jsonl` from implement automation).
- **No gender / semantics / tone rewrites** — do not change לך/לכם, phrasing, or customer-facing meaning unless operator explicitly asked.
- **Analyze (Grok) is read-only** — no code edits until Implement (Composer) webhook fires.

If the only fix you can imagine violates a ban → reply **`no action`** and explain why teaching is needed — **do not ship a dumb regex fix**.

## Commit tracking (implement only)

After push, run `scripts/log-qa-automation-commit.ts`. Operator briefs from `BRIEF.md`. Revert with `npm run qa:vanish -- <sha>`.

## Mandatory before commit/push

```bash
npm run guard:qa-fix
npm run verify:deploy
```

`guard:qa-fix:commit` runs on Vercel prebuild — **forbidden patterns block production deploy**.

False alarm (customer wanted rep, bot OK) → **`no action`**, zero diff.
